\title{Q1 2026}
\taxon{Log}
\date{2026-03-24}

\p{
    This has been a productive quarter. In early January we gave grants to Runtime Verification to test Hax for extracting code into Lean. They were successful in improving the tool, landing pull requests, and developing some good examples of (toy versions of) Rust programs of interest. Collaborating with them on this helped us see shortcomings in the Arklib specs and get a more realistic idea of what Rust verification could look like for us. Happily, our CompPoly specs did come in useful and they were able to verify some small Rust snippets against them.
}

\p{
    We settled on a roadmap for CompPoly in January, and while I and collaborators took CompPoly Phase 1 to the finish line, we put out a call for grants for Phase 2 of CompPoly. We got a lot of grant applications, and have just sent emails awarding grants for *all* of Phase 2. That should be done by the summer.
}

\p{
    We attended HACS and RWC26 in Taipei in early March, which was extremely productive. I learned a lot about Hax and Aeneas, verified compilers, and cryptography in general. Got strong insights for the upcoming work, and had a chance to evangelize our work on CompPoly. Bolton Bailey and I had a great conversation about the (many many) applications of computable polynomials in Lean. I hope that we can upstream CompPoly to CSLib and have many people using and maintaining it.
}

\p{
    Accomplishments:
    \ul{
        \li{CompPoly roadmap established and merged [in this pull request](https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/CompPoly/pull/16)}
        \li{Contributed a lot to CompPoly, established style guides and standards for contribution, integrated into CI, and built out a lot more theory with the help of collaborators, old and new.}
        \li{CompPoly Phase 1 of the Roadmap completed - see the [Zulip announcement](https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/523410-ArkLib/topic/CompPoly.20Phase.201.20Status/with/578352136)}
        \li{We have some basic examples of extraction from Rust to Lean (thank you RV) that we can hopefully build on.}
    }

    Events:
    \ul{
        \li{Giving two talks at EthCC[9], one (maybe two?) with Alex Hicks and one on my own.}
        \li{Invited to give a talk at SViL26 with Leo de Moura, Son Ho, and Karthikeyan Bhargavan in April.}
    }

    Next: I am responsible to see CompPoly make it through Phase 2 by the summer, though I will likely not be doing as much coding on it. Instead, I'll take a coordinating role and make sure the codebase fits together well and that the incoming code is high quality. We will likely have 8-10 contributors for Phase 2, which is exciting! This will be serious progress. We continue to integrate AI into our pipelines, successfully. I am currently looking for another chunk of technical work to do while I manage the CompPoly stuff, possibly contributing to [evm-asm](https://github.com/zksecurity/evm-asm).
}